From 63ac88dfe16541ee5a4e470a07761d36735219a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:51:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 069/108] gpu: vulkan: faster start - driver pipeline cache
 before the built-in pipelines, stored shaders translated in parallel

The driver pipeline cache file was merged only when the shader storage was
initialized, after the render target and texture caches had compiled their
built-in pipelines from scratch (~1.9 s per start on the Thor). It is now
merged at the start of the command processor setup (the only
*.vk.pipelinecache in the storage folder, since the title isn't known yet
there) and the storage reuses that merge. Vulkan setup 1.96 s -> 0.2 s.

Stored shader modifications are translated on worker threads (one shader
with all its modifications per work item, a translator per thread, the
binding layout map under a mutex): 580 -> 200 ms for 242 shaders, SPIR-V
byte-identical to the single-threaded translation. New cvar
vulkan_storage_translation_threads (-1 = creation thread count, 1 = serial).
Boot timing lines: 'Vulkan setup took', 'Shader storage loaded in'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

